      "value": "@{5f47de17bc82ac1e0f90f607|full_name}: Turns out that parallelization doesn't help much when the underlying methods aren't that performant to start with, and when the methods act on objects that depend on other objects in the hierarchy. When getting f(n) requires knowing the result of f(n-1) first, you can't make it parallel effectively.\ntl;dr: we looked into it, it isn't as easy as anyone had hoped, and simply \"using jobs\" doesn't really do that much. We'll circle back around to it eventually!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
